      "claim": "Perindopril, an ethyl ester prodrug, has high parent oral bioavailability (~65–75% in C10/C17/C18; additional L2 reports of 65–95% in C44/C53/C54/C68/C69/C80/C83/C90), supporting that the query's ester prodrug motif does not preclude F ≥ 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C10", "C17", "C18", "C44", "C53", "C54", "C68", "C69", "C80", "C83", "C90"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L2 records for perindoprilat show lower absolute F for the active metabolite (19±7% in young subjects, C35; 35±17% in elderly, C45), which is relevant context for prodrug conversion but does not change the parent-compound endpoint used for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C35", "C45"]
    }
  ],
